✅ Promise kya hota hai?
JavaScript mein Promise ek object hai jo future mein kisi asynchronous operation ka result batata hai — success ya failure.

📦 Ek promise bolta hai: "Main abhi kaam kar raha hoon, result baad mein dunga."

🔹 3 States of Promise:
Pending – Initial state, kaam chal raha hai

Fulfilled – Kaam successfully complete ho gaya

Rejected – Kaam fail ho gaya

🔹 Basic Syntax:
javascript

const promise = new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
  // async operation
  let success = true;

  if (success) {
    resolve("Kaam ho gaya!");
  } else {
    reject("Error aaya!");
  }
});
🔹 Use with .then() and .catch():
javascript

promise
  .then(result => {
    console.log("Success:", result);
  })
  .catch(error => {
    console.log("Fail:", error);
  });
✅ Real-world Example (API call):
javascript

fetch("https://api.example.com/data")
  .then(res => res.json())
  .then(data => console.log(data))
  .catch(err => console.log("Error:", err));
🔄 Comparison: Promise vs Callback
Callback Hell ❌	Promise ✅
Nested, hard to read	Clean chaining
Difficult error handling	Easy .catch()

🔁 Promise Summary Table:
Method	Use
.then()	Success result handle karne ke liye
.catch()	Error handle karne ke liye
.finally()	Hamesha chalega, success ya fail dono mein
